## 3. Cursor walk (add vs main)

  fixtures/lsp_cursor.oo has two functions. First `fn` is main (line 11).
  First `add(1, 2)` is the call in main. Offset 299. Line 12. Character 12.
  Comments do not contain `add(1, 2)` or `fn add`.
  lsp_ident_at at that offset is add. Not main. Not empty.
  lsp_fn_pos(src, "add") is `fn add` at line 16 character 4.
  First-fn-only hover would return markdown `fn main`.
  Cursor hover must return markdown `fn add`.
  Cursor definition must use `"line":16`. It must not use `"line":0`.

## 4. Product hover path

  textDocument/hover:
    name = lsp_ident_at(src, lsp_src_offset(src, line, col))
    empty name falls back to lsp_first_fn
    if lsp_fn_pos finds the name, value is `fn ` plus the name
  textDocument/definition:
    want = lsp_ident_at at the same offset
    range is lsp_fn_pos(want), else the first fn
  First-fn is only the empty-ident fallback. Not the add call.

